special_abilities:
  - name: "Demonic Devotion"
    description: "Every Blood Warrior makes a pact of devotion to an evil supernatural master (a Demon or Deevil Lord, or an evil deity of Hell or death), giving up his true name and bearing a ritual tattoo in Demongogian that marks his master and his rank. The master can summon him to his side at will once per day, appearing in an instant like a Dimensional Teleport, and can punish him at will as per the Agony spell, for as long as the master wishes and with no saving throw. He is -4 to save vs all curses and invocations of domination and intimidation (Charm, Charismatic Aura, Domination, Fear, Aura of Doom and the like) that come from his master; that penalty is conditional and is not added by the sheet."
  - name: "Mega-Damage Transformation"
    description: "The supernatural link makes him the equivalent of a minor supernatural being: his Hit Points and S.D.C. (including S.D.C. from skills) are added together and become his M.D.C. (the conversion is modelled). Add 1D6 M.D.C. per level of experience, starting at level one; the level-one 1D6 is in the class bonuses, and the sheet does not add the further 1D6 per level by itself. A character who is already a Mega-Damage being instead gains 1D6x10+40 M.D.C. from the link, plus either his race''s M.D.C. per level or 1D6 M.D.C. per level, whichever is greater; that alternative is not added by the sheet."
  - name: "Bio-Regeneration"
    description: "Recovers 2D6 M.D.C. per hour (48-288 every 24 hours)."
  - name: "Cannot Bleed Out"
    description: "Wounds clot and stop bleeding within two melee rounds (30 seconds), so he takes no additional damage from blood loss. Impervious to diseases that affect the blood."
  - name: "Temporary Eternal Torment Curse"
    description: "Can utter a curse that inflicts the effects of Eternal Torment temporarily: 10 minutes per level of the Blood Warrior (Tormented Dreams instead costs the victim one entire melee round and leaves the dream curse''s penalties). Costs 50 P.P.E., counts as two melee attacks and affects one person at a time; the victim must roll 13 or higher to save vs curse, and a successful save means no effect. See the Eternal Torment spell for the penalties."
  - name: "Spell Limitations"
    description: "His spells are not studied but awarded by his master. His focus is combat, so most spells should be offensive. A ritual takes him twice the normal time and 50% more P.P.E. For truly remarkable service the master may award 1D4 additional and/or higher level Blood spells or conventional invocations (up to level 10) as a special boon; those are added by hand."
  - name: "Death of the Master"
    description: "If his master is killed he can acquire no new spells unless another Demon Lord, Deevil Lord or dark deity accepts him, which is very unlikely. He loses half his M.D.C. and half his P.P.E., his spells cost twice as much P.P.E., and he is treated as a lowly, masterless Sub-Demon or Host."
trackable_resources: []
restrictions:
  - "The book presents this O.C.C. as a Non-Player Character villain and willing servant of evil, not intended as a player character. It is imported by Nate''s ruling of 2026-11-17 so a Game Master can build one; player use is at the Game Master''s discretion. A Blood Warrior who forsakes his master is summoned, tortured and slain or enslaved."
  - "Alignment: evil only. Aberrant (20%), Miscreant (40%) and Diabolic (40%)."
  - "Races are limited to those who can become spell casters."
  - "Cybernetics: none, and avoided at all costs because they interfere with his magic and Bio-Regeneration."
  - "+1 to Spell Strength at levels 6 and 12, not modeled. The +1 save vs mind control also covers mind-controlling drugs."
  - "Also starts with demonic leather armor (1D4x10+50 M.D.C.) styled with trophies from his kills, a Bone Weapon if he serves the demons of Hades or a Chrysteel weapon if he serves Dyval, one energy weapon of choice (a TW or Soulmancy weapon may be taken), one Soul Crystal, one slave or valet, and a whip (2D4 S.D.C. per lash) for punishments, plus 2D6x1,000 credits'' worth of Black Market goods over and above the coin in starting_money. He usually has the resources of the army or group he is assigned to."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames printed 88-91 (cache p089-p092, page_offset 1; cache p090 is a full-page illustration). Every figure was read off renders of cache 89, 91 and 92, which agreed with the text layer. The stats block opens ''Not intended as a player character. This is an NPC villain''; the class is imported as an ordinary published class by Nate''s ruling of 2026-11-17, with the warning carried as the first restriction and the evil tag (alignment is restricted to evil). occ_group magic and men_of_arms false: the section is headed ''Blood Warrior O.C.C. Magic Powers'', the same heading the Soulmancer carries, and his powers are spells endowed like a priest''s. Spells: Blood Armor and Blood Blade are granted by their catalog names; the class page prints them at 20 and 15 P.P.E. where the spell list prints 7 or 21 and 6, 12 or 18, and the catalog costs are not changed here. The four conventional invocations (Aura of Power, Cleanse, Death Trance, Globe of Daylight) are granted by name. Soulmancy picks draw from two named lists, the Soulmancy spells of levels 1-3 and of levels 1-7 as production holds them; spell_traditions_allowed is deliberately not stated, so the level-gated conventional picks (two from levels 1-2 at creation, one from levels 1-6 each level) reach general invocations only, exactly as the page grants. Experience Table printed 91. Base P.P.E. is ability 6. The M.D.C. conversion is mdc_from_hp_sdc with the level-one 1D6 as a pool bonus; the further 1D6 M.D.C. per level and the Mega-Damage-being alternative are prose in Mega-Damage Transformation. Literacy: Demongogian has no catalog row and is a Literacy: Other pick with its bonus. ''W.P.: Two Ancient'' and ''One Modern'' are Weapon Proficiencies picks with the split in their notes. Pilot ''Any except Robots and Power Armor'' excludes the robot and power armor rows by name; Military vehicles stay open. Science is Mathematics: Basic only. Equipment: the demonic symbol is the Holy Symbol row; the armor, the Bone or Chrysteel weapon, the energy weapon of choice, the Soul Crystal and the whip (no catalog whip does 2D4) are recorded in restrictions, not stubbed. Spell Strength and the conditional saves are prose."
---

## Lore

Blood Warriors are mortal men and women pledged to a Demon or Deevil Lord, or to a dark god of Hell or death, and deployed by both sides of the Minion War. They are warrior priests of a sort: not scholars of magic like the Soulmancer, but fighters endowed with Blood Magic and conventional spells by their master, gaining new ones as they rise in rank.

Among a master''s minions a Blood Warrior ranks with a Lesser Demon. They lead squads and platoons of mortal minions and Sub-Demons, sometimes even Lesser Demons, and are sent as special forces where a real demon would be the wrong tool, or where knowledge or subtlety is needed. Every one is evil, scarred by battle and Soulmancy, and covered in demonic tattoos.

## GM Notes

The book presents the Blood Warrior as an N.P.C. villain rather than a player character. A Blood Warrior who turns from his master is summoned to his side and destroyed or enslaved.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'blood-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'blood-warrior';

